.PP
Performs a best‑effort multi‑match search using Fibonacci probing\&. Although Fibonacci search is traditionally designed for locating a single target value in a sorted container, this method extends the algorithm to collect all elements for which the provided predicate returns a non‑strict match result\&.

.PP
Due to the nature of Fibonacci search — which discards large portions of the search space during probing — this method does not guarantee that all matching elements will be visited\&. It is intended for experimental or specialized use cases only\&.

.PP
In other words: only Bob can do this\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIcontainer\fP The container to search\&. Passed by reference to avoid copying\&. 
.br
\fIfunc\fP A callback that evaluates each probed element and returns a \fBCompareResult\fP describing its relation to the desired target\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
A \fBVector<T>\fP containing index/value pairs for all elements encountered during Fibonacci probing that satisfy the predicate\&. 
.RE
.PP

